title: The SPD Decides
subtitle: The Reichstag sits, and the Social Democrats must choose.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_cuno = 1 and crisis_time >= 1 and e23_cuno_spd = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.cunoTick(Q.crisis_time);
!}

= The SPD Decides

The Reichstag sits on the second day of the strike. Cuno reads a statement nobody listens to. In the lobbies the SPD deputies argue for hours: their own members are on strike under our slogans. If they keep Cuno, they lose the factories. If they bring him down, they will have to govern in his place.

Through an intermediary their Reichstag group asks what we would do if it voted against Cuno.

- @promise: Promise to end the strike once Cuno falls.
- @demand: Make a workers' government the price.
- @nothing: Promise nothing.

@promise
subtitle: The SPD withdraws its toleration today. When Cuno falls the strike ends, whatever else is possible then.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_cuno_spd = 1;
Q.e23_cuno_pressure += 25;
Q.spd_relation += 6;
RG.e22.cunoLines();
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

The intermediary takes our answer back. That evening the SPD group votes to withdraw its toleration of Cuno.

@demand
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The executive will refuse. Some of its deputies may not.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids offering the SPD a government.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.e23_cuno_spd = 2;
Q.e23_cuno_pressure += 10;
Q.e23_cuno_endurance += 6;
RG.e22.cunoLines();
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

The SPD executive says no. Thirty of its deputies say they would have said yes, and the strikers hear about both.

@nothing
subtitle: The strike keeps its edge. The SPD will call its own members back to work.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_cuno_spd = 3;
Q.e23_cuno_pressure += 5;
Q.e23_cuno_endurance -= 8;
Q.spd_relation -= 5;
RG.e22.cunoLines();
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Our deputies tell the intermediary to read *Die Rote Fahne*. The SPD calls on its members to go back to work, and some of them do.
